(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The module math's C-level algorithms of Modules/mathmodule.c (CPython 3.14.10; PY6g): m_log2, m_log10 and"] [10 1 "// loghelper over musl's log2 and log10, m_sinpi, the Lanczos gamma (lanczos_sum, m_tgamma, m_lgamma), the"] [11 1 "// double-length arithmetic (dl_*, tl_*), vector_norm (hypot, dist) and sumprod. As CPython is compiled on x86_64:"] [12 1 "// every float product rounded on its own (an explicit float64 conversion, so gc fuses no multiply-add on arm64),"] [13 1 "// fma C's correctly rounded one (math.FMA). The errno of the C code is the second result: 0, mathEDOM or mathERANGE."] [20 1 "// mLog2 is m_log2: special values handled, positive ones to musl's log2."] [37 1 "// mLog10 is m_log10."] [54 1 "// mLog is m_log."] [71 1 "// longFrexp is _PyLong_Frexp for a positive int: x in [0.5, 1) and e with n == x * 2**e, x rounded half to even."] [80 1 "// mathLoghelper is loghelper: an int by its value (a huge one through its frexp), else math_1 with the message"] [81 1 "// \"expected a positive input, got %s\"."] [98 3 "// 3.15.2's loghelper (queue 263): an __index__ whose int overflows a double goes through the int path"] [112 1 "// math1Result is math_1's checks of r = f(x) (errno never set by musl's functions)."] [133 1 "// math1aResult is math_1a: the function's errno decides (is_error)."] [152 1 "// mSinpi is m_sinpi: sin(pi*x) for finite x."] [215 1 "// mTgamma is m_tgamma."] [286 1 "// mLgamma is m_lgamma."] [315 1 "// the double-length arithmetic of mathmodule.c (dl_fast_sum, dl_sum, dl_mul by fma; tl_fma, tl_to_d)"] [348 1 "// vectorNorm is vector_norm: the Euclidean norm of vec (its items finite, |x| <= max) to within one ulp."] [388 1 "// mathAssignDouble is ASSIGN_DOUBLE: an exact float, an exact int by PyLong_AsDouble, else PyFloat_AsDouble."] [399 1 "// mathHypot is math_hypot."] [418 1 "// mathDist is math_dist_impl."] [459 1 "// mathSumprod is math_sumprod_impl: an exact int path (int64 without overflow), a float path of exact floats and"] [460 1 "// float/int pairs summed in triple length, and the generic p * q + total beyond."] [582 1 "// mathMaybeSpecial is _PyObject_MaybeCallSpecialNoArgs: o's type's special method called (its descriptor"] [583 1 "// bound), found false when the type has none."] [593 1 "// mathRound is math_floor and math_ceil: an exact float directly, else __floor__/__ceil__, else"] [594 1 "// PyFloat_AsDouble; PyLong_FromDouble of the result."] [618 1 "// mathTrunc is math_trunc."] [630 1 "// mathPermComb is math_perm and math_comb: n and k by __index__, arbitrary n, k (min(k, n - k) for comb) in C's"] [631 1 "// long long."] [638 28 "// math_factorial"] [684 1 "// mathNextafter is math_nextafter: musl's nextafter for one step (y when x == y), else CPython's steps."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[83 24] [87 29] [99 28] [202 14] [202 22] [207 13] [207 21] [390 24] [393 22] [453 24] [479 52] [597 25] [604 31] [620 25] [674 19] [674 27]] :go/trails [[188 54]]} (go/file "math_extra.go" :imports [


